menu "IPRO on-device tool-calling model"

config COMPONENTS_IPRO_LLM_ENABLE
    bool "ipro_llm engine: text request in, tool calls out"
    default n
    help
      Runs the IPRO SAN tool-calling models trained in tools/ipro_llm (XS:
      d192, 6 layers, CQ2/CQ4 weights, about 1.69 MB) from one blob made by
      tools/ipro_llm/export/export_blob.py. Portable C11 with no allocation:
      the app gives it the blob and about 1.5 MB of work memory (PSRAM, so
      it needs CONFIG_USE_PSRAM=y). Uses float; the IPRO7 FreeRTOS port
      saves the FPU registers, so other tasks may use float too.

config IPRO_LLM_NPU
    bool "Run the attention projections on the IPRO7 NPU"
    depends on COMPONENTS_IPRO_LLM_ENABLE && AI_SUPPORT
    default n
    help
      port/ipro7: q/k/v/gate and out of every layer become int8 1x1
      convolutions on the NPU, for prompt chunks and one-token decode
      steps (two models per projection). The blob needs the NPUS section
      (export_blob.py --npu-calib); the app attaches the accelerator with
      ipro_llm_npu_init() + ipro_llm_accel_attach(). About 1.2 MB of heap
      for XS (weights 0.9 MB, activation 256 KB). Needs CONFIG_AI_SUPPORT
      (the NPU runtime, components/ai).

config IPRO_LLM_PROF_CYCLES
    bool "Print the float work's cycle buckets after every request (debug)"
    depends on COMPONENTS_IPRO_LLM_ENABLE
    default n
    help
      Counts mcycle around the attention core (KV write, q/k norm + RoPE,
      softmax attention, sigmoid gate), the MLP (norms, FWHT, SiLU) and the
      engram, and prints one LLM_CYCLES line per ipro_llm_run(). Off, the
      buckets compile to nothing.

endmenu
